  m_Name: EVD_CaseFile
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TLA.Data::TLA.Data.Evidence.EvidenceDefinition
  evidenceId: EVD_CaseFile
  displayName: Case file 0147
  category: 0
  description: 'The initial incident report: the victim, the time he was found, who
    could get into the building and the persons of interest.'
  locationFound: "Evidence Room \xB7 investigation desk"
  interactionPrompt: Read case file
  pages:
  - "METROPOLITAN POLICE  \xB7  CASE 0147\nINCIDENT REPORT\n\nVictim: Daniel REYES,
    46. Co-owner of Reyes & Marlowe Architects, 3rd floor, 18 Harlow Street.\n\nReported
    23:52 on the 14th by Nora HAYES (office manager), who returned for her laptop
    and found the victim at his desk.\n\nFirst officer on scene 00:06. Victim pronounced
    dead at the scene."
  - 'SCENE


    Office door closed but not locked. No damage to door, frame or lock.

    Building
    alarm armed at 19:10. It never triggered.

    No sign of a struggle in the outer
    office.


    ACCESS


    Key holders: D. Reyes, E. Marlowe, N. Hayes.

    Card
    issued to V. Kim (dismissed two weeks ago) not yet deactivated.

    Building
    access log requested.'
  - "PERSONS OF INTEREST\n\nElliot MARLOWE, 51  \xB7  business partner. States he
    was at home all evening.\nNora HAYES, 34  \xB7  office manager. Found the body.\nVictor
    KIM, 29  \xB7  former junior architect. Dismissed after a dispute with the victim.\n\nNEXT
    STEPS\nInterview Marlowe. Obtain the building access log. Review lobby CCTV."
  image: {fileID: 0}
  caption: 
  examinationNotes: 'The access section is underlined twice in pencil: "Building
    access log requested." A copy should be in the filing cabinet by the shelves.'
  relatedFacts:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4b4bb222a9923df4f98ea8f17742221c, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5e013e8a921fc334db6b5c4d5e8ebe4d, type: 2}
  collectable: 1
  noteOnCollect: 'Reyes was found at 23:50 and the alarm never went off. Whoever
    was there had a key: Marlowe, Hayes or Kim.'
